@lang en
-- UNOFFICIAL TEXT. This is a plain-text reproduction, made by legalese commons, of the consolidation published by the King's Printer, Province of British Columbia (BC Laws). It is not an official version.
-- Source: https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/civix/document/id/complete/statreg/96238_01/xml (BC Laws consolidation, current to 2026-10-13).
-- These materials contain information that has been derived from information originally made available by the Province of British Columbia at: http://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca and this information is being used in accordance with the King's Printer Licence – British Columbia available at: https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/standards/Licence.html. They have not, however, been produced in affiliation with, or with the endorsement of, the Province of British Columbia and THESE MATERIALS ARE NOT AN OFFICIAL VERSION.
--
-- The Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238: the rules of reading an enactment and of the form
-- of its parts (ss 2(2), 2(3), 6, 7, 8, 8.1(2), 8.1(3), 9, 10, 11(1), 11(2), 12, 13, 15, 28(2) to (4), 30, 31, 33(2) to
-- (6), 39, 40, 42(1), 43 and 44).
-- Pass 2. Each rule is a function over a small typed representation of what the rule operates on: the kind of Act,
-- the part of an enactment, the word, the reference. Where the rule hands a judgment to the reader (which of two
-- constructions best ensures the objects of an enactment, whether a construction abrogates a right) the judgment is a
-- plain input. Where the text does not say, the answer is a named REFUSE.
--
-- Every rule here is subject to s 2(1): a provision of the Act applies unless a contrary intention appears in the Act or
-- in the enactment. The caller applies `s 2(1) a provision of this Act applies to an enactment`, in
-- `bc-interpretation-definitions.l4`, before relying on an answer; no rule in this file takes that input (NOTES.md,
-- finding 3).
--
-- What FALSE and REFUSE mean here (NOTES.md, finding 2). TRUE: the case is within the provision and the provision gives the
-- thing. FALSE: only where the words of the provision give the negative themselves (an exception, "is not part", a limit
-- such as "so far as it is applicable"). REFUSE: the case is outside what the provision speaks of, or the provision only
-- permits or "includes" and the case is not listed; the text is silent and a default would be a guess.
--
-- Draft. A single Sonnet 5.5 agent wrote this from the text alone; no domain expert has read it
-- against the statute. The quotations are copied from `RSBC-1996-c.-238.txt`, a plain-text
-- rendering made by a script (not the official text), by `srcrefs.py`; `src:N` is line N of that file.
--
-- Target compiler: `unstable` (REFUSE and YMD are rejected by `main`).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-definitions`

§ `s 2 Application`

DECLARE `The enactment a provision of this Act is applied to` IS ONE OF
    `This Act`
    `Another enactment`

-- src:21 | (2) The provisions of this Act apply to this Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 2(2) (src:21)
GIVEN enactment IS A `The enactment a provision of this Act is applied to`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(2) the provisions of this Act apply to the enactment` enactment MEANS
    CONSIDER enactment
        WHEN `This Act` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Another enactment` THEN `s 2(2) speaks only of this Act; s 2(1) governs another enactment`

-- src:21 | (2) The provisions of this Act apply to this Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 2(2) (src:21)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(2) speaks only of this Act; s 2(1) governs another enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 2(2) speaks only of this Act; s 2(1) governs another enactment"

-- src:22 | (3) Nothing in this Act excludes the application to an enactment of a rule of construction applicable to it and not inconsistent with this Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 2(3) (src:22)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(3) speaks only of a rule of construction that is applicable to the enactment and not inconsistent with this Act` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 2(3) speaks only of a rule of construction that is applicable to the enactment and not inconsistent with this Act"

-- src:22 | (3) Nothing in this Act excludes the application to an enactment of a rule of construction applicable to it and not inconsistent with this Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 2(3) (src:22)
GIVEN `the rule of construction is applicable to the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rule is inconsistent with this Act`                 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(3) a rule of construction is preserved by this Act` `the rule of construction is applicable to the enactment` `the rule is inconsistent with this Act` MEANS
    IF   `the rule of construction is applicable to the enactment` AND (NOT `the rule is inconsistent with this Act`)
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `s 2(3) speaks only of a rule of construction that is applicable to the enactment and not inconsistent with this Act`

§ `s 6 Effect of private Acts`

DECLARE `Kind of Act` IS ONE OF
    `A private Act`
    `Any other Act`

DECLARE `What s 6 says a provision does to a person's right` IS ONE OF
    `The provision does not affect the right`
    `The provision affects the right only as the Act refers to or mentions it`

-- src:47 | 6 A provision in a private Act does not affect the rights of any person, except only as referred to or mentioned in that Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 6 (src:47)
GIVETH A `What s 6 says a provision does to a person's right`
`s 6 speaks only of a provision in a private Act` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 6 speaks only of a provision in a private Act"

-- src:47 | 6 A provision in a private Act does not affect the rights of any person, except only as referred to or mentioned in that Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 6 (src:47)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act`
      `the Act refers to or mentions the right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What s 6 says a provision does to a person's right`
`s 6 what a provision in an Act does to a person's right` kind `the Act refers to or mentions the right` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `A private Act` THEN
            IF   `the Act refers to or mentions the right`
            THEN `The provision affects the right only as the Act refers to or mentions it`
            ELSE `The provision does not affect the right`
        WHEN `Any other Act` THEN `s 6 speaks only of a provision in a private Act`

§ `s 7 Enactment always speaking`

-- src:50 | 7 (1) Every enactment must be construed as always speaking.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 7(1) (src:50)
GIVEN `the day the enactment was enacted` IS A DATE
      `the day the enactment is applied`  IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 7(1) the day as of which an enactment is read` `the day the enactment was enacted` `the day the enactment is applied` MEANS
    `the day the enactment is applied`

DECLARE `Tense of a provision` IS ONE OF
    `Present tense`
    `Another tense`

-- src:51 | (2) If a provision in an enactment is expressed in the present tense, the provision applies to the circumstances as they arise.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 7(2) (src:51)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 7(2) speaks only of a provision expressed in the present tense` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 7(2) speaks only of a provision expressed in the present tense"

-- src:51 | (2) If a provision in an enactment is expressed in the present tense, the provision applies to the circumstances as they arise.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 7(2) (src:51)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 7(2) does not say whether a provision applies to a circumstance that arises while the enactment is not in force` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 7(2) does not say whether a provision applies to a circumstance that arises while the enactment is not in force"

-- src:51 | (2) If a provision in an enactment is expressed in the present tense, the provision applies to the circumstances as they arise.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 7(2) (src:51)
GIVEN tense IS A `Tense of a provision`
      `the circumstance arises while the enactment is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 7(2) the provision applies to the circumstance as it arises` tense `the circumstance arises while the enactment is in force` MEANS
    CONSIDER tense
        WHEN `Present tense` THEN
            IF   `the circumstance arises while the enactment is in force`
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE `s 7(2) does not say whether a provision applies to a circumstance that arises while the enactment is not in force`
        WHEN `Another tense` THEN `s 7(2) speaks only of a provision expressed in the present tense`

§ `s 8 Enactment remedial`

-- "such fair, large and liberal construction and interpretation as best ensures the attainment of its objects" is a
-- judgment, so it is an input: for each candidate construction, whether it best ensures the attainment of the objects.
DECLARE `A candidate construction` HAS
    `its label` IS A STRING
    `it best ensures the attainment of the objects of the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:54 | 8 Every enactment must be construed as being remedial, and must be given such fair, large and liberal construction and interpretation as best ensures the attainment of its objects.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 8 (src:54)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 8 names no construction when none is said to best ensure the attainment of the objects` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 8 names no construction when none is said to best ensure the attainment of the objects"

-- src:54 | 8 Every enactment must be construed as being remedial, and must be given such fair, large and liberal construction and interpretation as best ensures the attainment of its objects.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 8 (src:54)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 8 does not choose between constructions that equally best ensure the attainment of the objects` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 8 does not choose between constructions that equally best ensure the attainment of the objects"

-- src:54 | 8 Every enactment must be construed as being remedial, and must be given such fair, large and liberal construction and interpretation as best ensures the attainment of its objects.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 8 (src:54)
GIVEN candidates IS A LIST OF `A candidate construction`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 8 the construction to give to an enactment` candidates MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `it best ensures the attainment of the objects of the enactment`) candidates
        WHEN EMPTY THEN `s 8 names no construction when none is said to best ensure the attainment of the objects`
        WHEN best FOLLOWED BY others THEN
            IF   null others
            THEN best's `its label`
            ELSE `s 8 does not choose between constructions that equally best ensure the attainment of the objects`

§ `s 8.1 Section 35 of the Constitution Act, 1982 and the Declaration`

-- src:61 | (2) For certainty, every enactment must be construed as upholding and not abrogating or derogating from the aboriginal and treaty rights of Indigenous peoples as recognized and affirmed by section 35 of the Constitution Act, 1982.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 8.1(2) (src:61)
GIVEN `the construction abrogates or derogates from the aboriginal and treaty rights of Indigenous peoples as recognized and affirmed by section 35 of the Constitution Act, 1982` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8.1(2) a construction of an enactment is open` `the construction abrogates or derogates from the aboriginal and treaty rights of Indigenous peoples as recognized and affirmed by section 35 of the Constitution Act, 1982` MEANS
    NOT `the construction abrogates or derogates from the aboriginal and treaty rights of Indigenous peoples as recognized and affirmed by section 35 of the Constitution Act, 1982`

DECLARE `Kind of enactment` IS ONE OF
    `An Act`
    `A regulation`
    `An enactment that is neither an Act nor a regulation`

-- src:62 | (3) Every Act and regulation must be construed as being consistent with the Declaration.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 8.1(3) (src:62)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8.1(3) speaks only of an Act and a regulation` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 8.1(3) speaks only of an Act and a regulation"

-- src:62 | (3) Every Act and regulation must be construed as being consistent with the Declaration.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 8.1(3) (src:62)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of enactment`
      `the construction is consistent with the Declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8.1(3) a construction of the enactment is open` kind `the construction is consistent with the Declaration` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `An Act` THEN `the construction is consistent with the Declaration`
        WHEN `A regulation` THEN `the construction is consistent with the Declaration`
        WHEN `An enactment that is neither an Act nor a regulation` THEN `s 8.1(3) speaks only of an Act and a regulation`

§ `s 9 and s 11 The parts of an enactment`

DECLARE `Part of an enactment, or printed with it` IS ONE OF
    `The title`
    `The preamble`
    `A head note to a provision`
    `A reference after the end of a section or other division`
    `Text in square brackets after a reference to a provision`
        HAS `it is italicized`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
            `it is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Any other part`

-- src:65 | 9 The title and preamble of an enactment are part of it and are intended to assist in explaining its meaning and object.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 9 (src:65)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9 speaks only of the title and the preamble` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 9 speaks only of the title and the preamble"

-- src:65 | 9 The title and preamble of an enactment are part of it and are intended to assist in explaining its meaning and object.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 9 (src:65)
GIVEN part IS A `Part of an enactment, or printed with it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9 the part is part of the enactment` part MEANS
    CONSIDER part
        WHEN `The title` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `The preamble` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `s 9 speaks only of the title and the preamble`

-- src:65 | 9 The title and preamble of an enactment are part of it and are intended to assist in explaining its meaning and object.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 9 (src:65)
GIVEN part IS A `Part of an enactment, or printed with it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9 the part is intended to assist in explaining the meaning and object of the enactment` part MEANS
    CONSIDER part
        WHEN `The title` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `The preamble` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `s 9 speaks only of the title and the preamble`

-- src:74 | (2) In an enactment, if a reference to a provision of the enactment or any other enactment is followed by italicized text in square brackets that is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision, subsection (1) (a) and (b) applies to the text in square brackets.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 11(2) (src:74)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(2) speaks only of italicized text in square brackets, after a reference to a provision, that is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 11(2) speaks only of italicized text in square brackets, after a reference to a provision, that is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision"

-- src:74 | (2) In an enactment, if a reference to a provision of the enactment or any other enactment is followed by italicized text in square brackets that is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision, subsection (1) (a) and (b) applies to the text in square brackets.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 11(2) (src:74)
GIVEN `it follows a reference to a provision of the enactment or any other enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is italicized`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(2) subsection (1)(a) and (b) apply to the text in square brackets` `it follows a reference to a provision of the enactment or any other enactment` `it is italicized` `it is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision` MEANS
    IF       `it follows a reference to a provision of the enactment or any other enactment`
         AND `it is italicized`
         AND `it is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `s 11(2) speaks only of italicized text in square brackets, after a reference to a provision, that is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision`

-- src:71 | 11 (1) In an enactment, a head note to a provision or a reference after the end of a section or other division
-- src:72 | (a) is not part of the enactment, and
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 11(1)(a) (src:71-72)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(1) speaks only of a head note, a reference after the end of a section or division, and text in square brackets` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 11(1) speaks only of a head note, a reference after the end of a section or division, and text in square brackets"

-- src:71 | 11 (1) In an enactment, a head note to a provision or a reference after the end of a section or other division
-- src:72 | (a) is not part of the enactment, and
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 11(1)(a) (src:71-72)
GIVEN part IS A `Part of an enactment, or printed with it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` part MEANS
    CONSIDER part
        WHEN `A head note to a provision` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `A reference after the end of a section or other division` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `Text in square brackets after a reference to a provision` italicized descriptive THEN
            NOT (`s 11(2) subsection (1)(a) and (b) apply to the text in square brackets` TRUE italicized descriptive)
        OTHERWISE `s 11(1) speaks only of a head note, a reference after the end of a section or division, and text in square brackets`

-- src:71 | 11 (1) In an enactment, a head note to a provision or a reference after the end of a section or other division
-- src:72 | (a) is not part of the enactment, and
-- src:73 | (b) must be considered to have been added editorially for convenience of reference only.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 11(1)(b) (src:71-73)
GIVEN part IS A `Part of an enactment, or printed with it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(1)(b) the part must be considered to have been added editorially for convenience of reference only` part MEANS
    CONSIDER part
        WHEN `A head note to a provision` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A reference after the end of a section or other division` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Text in square brackets after a reference to a provision` italicized descriptive THEN
            `s 11(2) subsection (1)(a) and (b) apply to the text in square brackets` TRUE italicized descriptive
        OTHERWISE `s 11(1) speaks only of a head note, a reference after the end of a section or division, and text in square brackets`

-- src:65 | 9 The title and preamble of an enactment are part of it and are intended to assist in explaining its meaning and object.
-- src:71 | 11 (1) In an enactment, a head note to a provision or a reference after the end of a section or other division
-- src:72 | (a) is not part of the enactment, and
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 9 and s 11(1)(a) (src:65 and src:71-72)
GIVEN part IS A `Part of an enactment, or printed with it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9 and s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` part MEANS
    CONSIDER part
        WHEN `The title` THEN `s 9 the part is part of the enactment` part
        WHEN `The preamble` THEN `s 9 the part is part of the enactment` part
        OTHERWISE `s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` part

§ `s 10 Enacting clause`

-- The text says an enacting clause "may be in the following form". It does not say a clause in another form is
-- not allowed, so the answer for another form is a refusal, not FALSE (NOTES.md, fork F-open-list).
-- src:68 | 10 The enacting clause of an Act of the Legislature may be in the following form: "Her Majesty, by and with the advice and consent of the Legislative Assembly of the Province of British Columbia, enacts as follows:".
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 10 (src:68)
GIVETH A STRING
`the form of enacting clause that s 10 gives` MEANS
    "Her Majesty, by and with the advice and consent of the Legislative Assembly of the Province of British Columbia, enacts as follows:"

-- src:68 | 10 The enacting clause of an Act of the Legislature may be in the following form: "Her Majesty, by and with the advice and consent of the Legislative Assembly of the Province of British Columbia, enacts as follows:".
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 10 (src:68)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10 does not say that an enacting clause in another form is not allowed` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 10 says only that the enacting clause of an Act may be in the form given; it does not say that another form is not allowed"

-- src:68 | 10 The enacting clause of an Act of the Legislature may be in the following form: "Her Majesty, by and with the advice and consent of the Legislative Assembly of the Province of British Columbia, enacts as follows:".
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 10 (src:68)
GIVEN clause IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10 the enacting clause of an Act of the Legislature may be in this form` clause MEANS
    IF   clause EQUALS `the form of enacting clause that s 10 gives`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `s 10 does not say that an enacting clause in another form is not allowed`

§ `s 12 Definitions and interpretation provisions`

DECLARE `Place where a definition or interpretation provision is applied` IS ONE OF
    `In the section containing the definition or interpretation provision`
    `In another part of the enactment`
    `In another enactment`

-- src:78 | 12 Definitions or interpretation provisions in an enactment, unless the contrary intention appears in the enactment, apply to the whole enactment including the section containing a definition or interpretation provision.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 12 (src:78)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12 speaks only of the enactment that contains the definition or interpretation provision` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 12 speaks only of the enactment that contains the definition or interpretation provision"

-- src:78 | 12 Definitions or interpretation provisions in an enactment, unless the contrary intention appears in the enactment, apply to the whole enactment including the section containing a definition or interpretation provision.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 12 (src:78)
GIVEN place IS A `Place where a definition or interpretation provision is applied`
      `the contrary intention appears in the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12 the definition or interpretation provision applies in the place` place `the contrary intention appears in the enactment` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
        WHEN `In the section containing the definition or interpretation provision` THEN NOT `the contrary intention appears in the enactment`
        WHEN `In another part of the enactment` THEN NOT `the contrary intention appears in the enactment`
        WHEN `In another enactment` THEN `s 12 speaks only of the enactment that contains the definition or interpretation provision`

§ `s 13 Expressions in regulations`

-- src:81 | 13 An expression used in a regulation has the same meaning as in the enactment authorizing the regulation.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 13 (src:81)
GIVEN `the meaning of the expression in the enactment authorizing the regulation, if it has one` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 13 the meaning of an expression used in a regulation` `the meaning of the expression in the enactment authorizing the regulation, if it has one` MEANS
    `the meaning of the expression in the enactment authorizing the regulation, if it has one`

§ `s 15 Power of repeal and amendment`

DECLARE `Something the Legislature may do to an Act` IS ONE OF
    `Repeal it`
    `Amend it`
    `Revoke a power, privilege or advantage that it vests in or grants to a person`
    `Restrict a power, privilege or advantage that it vests in or grants to a person`
    `Modify a power, privilege or advantage that it vests in or grants to a person`

-- src:88 | 15 (1) Every Act must be construed as to reserve to the Legislature the power of repealing or amending it, and of revoking, restricting or modifying a power, privilege or advantage that it vests in or grants to any person.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 15(1) (src:88)
GIVEN thing IS A `Something the Legislature may do to an Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(1) the Act is construed as reserving to the Legislature the power` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `Repeal it` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Amend it` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Revoke a power, privilege or advantage that it vests in or grants to a person` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Restrict a power, privilege or advantage that it vests in or grants to a person` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Modify a power, privilege or advantage that it vests in or grants to a person` THEN TRUE

-- src:89 | (2) An Act may be amended or repealed by an Act passed in the same session of the Legislature.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 15(2) (src:89)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(2) speaks only of an Act passed in the same session of the Legislature; s 15(1) reserves the power generally` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 15(2) speaks only of an Act passed in the same session of the Legislature; s 15(1) reserves the power generally"

-- src:89 | (2) An Act may be amended or repealed by an Act passed in the same session of the Legislature.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 15(2) (src:89)
GIVEN `the amending or repealing Act is passed in the same session of the Legislature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(2) an Act may be amended or repealed by an Act passed in the same session` `the amending or repealing Act is passed in the same session of the Legislature` MEANS
    IF   `the amending or repealing Act is passed in the same session of the Legislature`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `s 15(2) speaks only of an Act passed in the same session of the Legislature; s 15(1) reserves the power generally`

§ `s 28 Use of words`

DECLARE `Who a gender specific term is applied to` IS ONE OF
    `A person of any gender`
    `A corporation`
    `Something that is neither a person nor a corporation`

-- src:217 | (2) Gender specific terms include all genders and include corporations.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 28(2) (src:217)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(2) speaks only of persons of any gender and corporations` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 28(2) speaks only of persons of any gender and corporations"

-- src:217 | (2) Gender specific terms include all genders and include corporations.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 28(2) (src:217)
GIVEN who IS A `Who a gender specific term is applied to`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(2) a gender specific term includes` who MEANS
    CONSIDER who
        WHEN `A person of any gender` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A corporation` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Something that is neither a person nor a corporation` THEN `s 28(2) speaks only of persons of any gender and corporations`

DECLARE `Grammatical number` IS ONE OF
    `Singular`
    `Plural`

-- src:218 | (3) In an enactment words in the singular include the plural, and words in the plural include the singular.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 28(3) (src:218)
GIVEN `the number the word is written in` IS A `Grammatical number`
      `the number the question is about`  IS A `Grammatical number`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(3) a word in one number includes the other number` `the number the word is written in` `the number the question is about` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the number the word is written in`
        WHEN `Singular` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Plural` THEN TRUE

-- src:219 | (4) If a word or expression is defined in an enactment, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the same word or expression have corresponding meanings.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 28(4) (src:219)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(4) speaks only of another part of speech or grammatical form of a word or expression defined in the enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 28(4) speaks only of another part of speech or grammatical form of a word or expression defined in the enactment"

-- src:219 | (4) If a word or expression is defined in an enactment, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the same word or expression have corresponding meanings.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 28(4) (src:219)
GIVEN `the word or expression is defined in the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form is another part of speech or grammatical form of the same word or expression` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(4) the form has a corresponding meaning` `the word or expression is defined in the enactment` `the form is another part of speech or grammatical form of the same word or expression` MEANS
    IF       `the word or expression is defined in the enactment`
         AND `the form is another part of speech or grammatical form of the same word or expression`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `s 28(4) speaks only of another part of speech or grammatical form of a word or expression defined in the enactment`

§ `s 30 Metric expressions`

-- src:357 | 30 In an enactment, metric expressions and symbols have the meaning given to them in the Weights and Measures Act (Canada) and if not mentioned there, have the meaning given to them in the International System of Units established by the General Conference of Weights and Measures.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 30 (src:357)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 30 gives no meaning to a metric expression that neither source gives a meaning to` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 30 gives no meaning to a metric expression that neither the Weights and Measures Act (Canada) nor the International System of Units gives a meaning to"

-- src:357 | 30 In an enactment, metric expressions and symbols have the meaning given to them in the Weights and Measures Act (Canada) and if not mentioned there, have the meaning given to them in the International System of Units established by the General Conference of Weights and Measures.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 30 (src:357)
GIVEN `the meaning given in the Weights and Measures Act (Canada), if it is mentioned there` IS A MAYBE STRING
      `the meaning given in the International System of Units, if it is mentioned there` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 30 the meaning of a metric expression or symbol` `the meaning given in the Weights and Measures Act (Canada), if it is mentioned there` `the meaning given in the International System of Units, if it is mentioned there` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the meaning given in the Weights and Measures Act (Canada), if it is mentioned there`
        WHEN JUST meaning THEN meaning
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            CONSIDER `the meaning given in the International System of Units, if it is mentioned there`
                WHEN JUST meaning THEN meaning
                WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 30 gives no meaning to a metric expression that neither source gives a meaning to`

§ `s 31 Common names`

-- src:360 | 31 In an enactment, the name commonly applied to a country, place, body, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing means the country, place, body, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing to which the name is commonly applied, although the name is not the formal or extended designation of it.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 31 (src:360)
GIVEN `the name` IS A STRING
      `the country, place, body, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing to which the name is commonly applied` IS A STRING
      `the formal or extended designation of that thing` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 31 what the commonly applied name means` `the name` `the country, place, body, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing to which the name is commonly applied` `the formal or extended designation of that thing` MEANS
    `the country, place, body, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing to which the name is commonly applied`

§ `s 33 References in enactments`

DECLARE `What a reference in an enactment is to` IS ONE OF
    `A Part`
    `A division`
    `A section`
    `A schedule`
    `An appendix`
    `A form`
    `A subsection`
    `A paragraph`
    `A subparagraph`
    `A clause`

DECLARE `Where a reference occurs` IS ONE OF
    `In a section`
    `In a subsection`
    `In a paragraph`
    `In a subparagraph`

-- src:376 | (2) A reference in an enactment to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix, or form is a reference to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form of the enactment in which the reference occurs.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 33(2) (src:376)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 33(2) speaks only of a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 33(2) speaks only of a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form"

-- src:376 | (2) A reference in an enactment to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix, or form is a reference to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form of the enactment in which the reference occurs.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 33(2) (src:376)
GIVEN what IS A `What a reference in an enactment is to`
      `the enactment in which the reference occurs` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 33(2) the enactment a reference to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form is a reference into` what `the enactment in which the reference occurs` MEANS
    CONSIDER what
        WHEN `A Part` THEN `the enactment in which the reference occurs`
        WHEN `A division` THEN `the enactment in which the reference occurs`
        WHEN `A section` THEN `the enactment in which the reference occurs`
        WHEN `A schedule` THEN `the enactment in which the reference occurs`
        WHEN `An appendix` THEN `the enactment in which the reference occurs`
        WHEN `A form` THEN `the enactment in which the reference occurs`
        OTHERWISE `s 33(2) speaks only of a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form`

-- src:377 | (3) A reference in an enactment to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause is a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause of the section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph in which the reference occurs.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 33(3) (src:377)
GIVETH A `Where a reference occurs`
`s 33(3) speaks only of a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 33(3) speaks only of a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause"

-- src:377 | (3) A reference in an enactment to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause is a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause of the section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph in which the reference occurs.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 33(3) (src:377)
GIVEN what IS A `What a reference in an enactment is to`
      place IS A `Where a reference occurs`
GIVETH A `Where a reference occurs`
`s 33(3) the section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause is a reference into` what place MEANS
    CONSIDER what
        WHEN `A subsection` THEN place
        WHEN `A paragraph` THEN place
        WHEN `A subparagraph` THEN place
        WHEN `A clause` THEN place
        OTHERWISE `s 33(3) speaks only of a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause`

-- src:378 | (4) A reference in an enactment to regulations is a reference to regulations made under the enactment in which the reference occurs.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 33(4) (src:378)
GIVEN `the enactment under which the regulations were made` IS A STRING
      `the enactment in which the reference occurs`         IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(4) a reference to regulations is a reference to these regulations` `the enactment under which the regulations were made` `the enactment in which the reference occurs` MEANS
    `the enactment under which the regulations were made` EQUALS `the enactment in which the reference occurs`

-- src:379 | (5) A reference in an enactment by number or letter to a section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause or other division or line of another enactment must be construed as a reference to the division or line of the other enactment as printed under the King's Printer Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 33(5) (src:379)
GIVEN `the division or line as printed under the King's Printer Act` IS A STRING
      `the division or line as numbered in another version`         IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 33(5) the division or line of the other enactment a reference by number or letter is a reference to` `the division or line as printed under the King's Printer Act` `the division or line as numbered in another version` MEANS
    `the division or line as printed under the King's Printer Act`

DECLARE `An instrument a reference under a named or unnamed Act might be to` IS ONE OF
    `The Act itself`
    `A regulation enacted under the authority of that Act`
    `A regulation enacted under the authority of another Act`

-- "includes" leaves the list open (the terms module's rule, NOTES.md fork F-open-list): a regulation under another Act is
-- not listed, so the answer for it is a refusal, not FALSE.
-- src:380 | (6) If an enactment refers to a matter "under" a named or unnamed Act, an Act in that reference includes regulations enacted under the authority of that Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 33(6) (src:380)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(6) says what an Act in that reference includes and does not say what it leaves out` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 33(6) says an Act in that reference includes regulations enacted under the authority of that Act; it does not say what else it includes or leaves out"

-- src:380 | (6) If an enactment refers to a matter "under" a named or unnamed Act, an Act in that reference includes regulations enacted under the authority of that Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 33(6) (src:380)
GIVEN instrument IS A `An instrument a reference under a named or unnamed Act might be to`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(6) an Act in a reference to a matter under an Act includes the instrument` instrument MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
        WHEN `The Act itself` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A regulation enacted under the authority of that Act` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A regulation enacted under the authority of another Act` THEN `s 33(6) says what an Act in that reference includes and does not say what it leaves out`

§ `s 39 and s 40 Definitions in other Acts`

-- src:413 | 39 The definitions section of the Supreme Court Act, so far as the terms defined can be applied, extends to all enactments relating to legal proceedings.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 39 (src:413)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39 speaks only of an enactment relating to legal proceedings` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 39 speaks only of an enactment relating to legal proceedings"

-- "so far as the terms defined can be applied" is a limit in the words of the section, so a term that cannot be applied
-- gets FALSE; an enactment that does not relate to legal proceedings is outside what the section speaks of, so it gets a refusal.
-- src:413 | 39 The definitions section of the Supreme Court Act, so far as the terms defined can be applied, extends to all enactments relating to legal proceedings.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 39 (src:413)
GIVEN `the enactment relates to legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term defined can be applied`            IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39 the definitions section of the Supreme Court Act extends to the term in the enactment` `the enactment relates to legal proceedings` `the term defined can be applied` MEANS
    IF   `the enactment relates to legal proceedings`
    THEN `the term defined can be applied`
    ELSE `s 39 speaks only of an enactment relating to legal proceedings`

DECLARE `Source of definitions for municipal and regional district matters` IS ONE OF
    `The Schedule to the Community Charter`
    `Section 1 of the Schedule to the Local Government Act`

-- src:416 | 40 (1) So far as the terms defined can be applied, the definitions established by or applicable under the following apply to all enactments relating to municipal and regional district matters:
-- src:417 | (a) the Schedule to the Community Charter;
-- src:418 | (b) section 1 of the Schedule to the Local Government Act.
-- src:419 | (2) As an exception, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the definition of "municipality" in the Community Charter.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 40 (src:416-419)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40 speaks only of an enactment relating to municipal and regional district matters` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 40 speaks only of an enactment relating to municipal and regional district matters"

-- src:416 | 40 (1) So far as the terms defined can be applied, the definitions established by or applicable under the following apply to all enactments relating to municipal and regional district matters:
-- src:417 | (a) the Schedule to the Community Charter;
-- src:418 | (b) section 1 of the Schedule to the Local Government Act.
-- src:419 | (2) As an exception, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the definition of "municipality" in the Community Charter.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 40 (src:416-419)
GIVEN source IS A `Source of definitions for municipal and regional district matters`
      term   IS A STRING
      `the enactment relates to municipal and regional district matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term defined can be applied`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40 the definition applies to the term in the enactment` source term `the enactment relates to municipal and regional district matters` `the term defined can be applied` MEANS
    IF   `the enactment relates to municipal and regional district matters`
    THEN     `the term defined can be applied`
         AND NOT (source EQUALS `The Schedule to the Community Charter` AND term EQUALS "municipality")
    ELSE `s 40 speaks only of an enactment relating to municipal and regional district matters`

§ `s 42(1) Subdivisions of an Act`

-- src:432 | 42 (1) A section is divided into subdivisions known in descending order as subsections, paragraphs, subparagraphs and clauses.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 42(1) (src:432)
GIVEN subdivision IS A `Subdivision of a section`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 42(1) the place of a subdivision in the descending order` subdivision MEANS
    CONSIDER subdivision
        WHEN Subsection THEN 1
        WHEN Paragraph THEN 2
        WHEN Subparagraph THEN 3
        WHEN Clause THEN 4

-- src:432 | 42 (1) A section is divided into subdivisions known in descending order as subsections, paragraphs, subparagraphs and clauses.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 42(1) (src:432)
GIVEN subdivision IS A `Subdivision of a section`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Subdivision of a section`
`s 42(1) the subdivision next below` subdivision MEANS
    CONSIDER subdivision
        WHEN Subsection THEN JUST Paragraph
        WHEN Paragraph THEN JUST Subparagraph
        WHEN Subparagraph THEN JUST Clause
        WHEN Clause THEN NOTHING

§ `s 43 Citation of Acts`

DECLARE `Kind of Act, for citing it` IS ONE OF
    `An Act that is neither a revised statute in a general revision nor a limited revision`
    `A revised statute included in a general revision`
    `An Act that is a limited revision`

DECLARE `A way of citing an Act` IS ONE OF
    `By its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted`
    `By its title, with or without its chapter number`
    `By its chapter number in the Revised Statutes of British Columbia`
    `By its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted and as a Revised Statute of British Columbia for that year`
    `In some other way`

-- src:439 | 43 An Act may be cited as follows:
-- src:440 | (a) by reference to its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted;
-- src:441 | (b) by reference to its title, with or without reference to its chapter number;
-- src:442 | (c) in the case of an Act that is a revised statute included in a general revision, by reference to its chapter number in the Revised Statutes of British Columbia;
-- src:443 | (d) in the case of an Act that is a limited revision, by reference to its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted and as a Revised Statute of British Columbia for that year.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 43 (src:439-443)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43 says only how an Act may be cited; it does not say that another way is not allowed` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 43 says only how an Act may be cited; it does not say that another way is not allowed"

-- src:439 | 43 An Act may be cited as follows:
-- src:440 | (a) by reference to its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted;
-- src:441 | (b) by reference to its title, with or without reference to its chapter number;
-- src:442 | (c) in the case of an Act that is a revised statute included in a general revision, by reference to its chapter number in the Revised Statutes of British Columbia;
-- src:443 | (d) in the case of an Act that is a limited revision, by reference to its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted and as a Revised Statute of British Columbia for that year.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 43 (src:439-443)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act, for citing it`
      way  IS A `A way of citing an Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43 an Act of this kind may be cited this way` kind way MEANS
    CONSIDER way
        WHEN `By its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `By its title, with or without its chapter number` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `By its chapter number in the Revised Statutes of British Columbia` THEN
            IF   kind EQUALS `A revised statute included in a general revision`
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE `s 43 says only how an Act may be cited; it does not say that another way is not allowed`
        WHEN `By its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted and as a Revised Statute of British Columbia for that year` THEN
            IF   kind EQUALS `An Act that is a limited revision`
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE `s 43 says only how an Act may be cited; it does not say that another way is not allowed`
        WHEN `In some other way` THEN `s 43 says only how an Act may be cited; it does not say that another way is not allowed`

§ `s 44 Mutatis mutandis`

-- src:446 | 44 If an enactment provides that another enactment applies, it applies with the necessary changes and so far as it is applicable.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 44 (src:446)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44 speaks only of an enactment that provides that another enactment applies` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 44 speaks only of an enactment that provides that another enactment applies"

-- "so far as it is applicable" and "the necessary changes" are limits in the words of the section: FALSE when unmet.
-- src:446 | 44 If an enactment provides that another enactment applies, it applies with the necessary changes and so far as it is applicable.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 44 (src:446)
GIVEN `the enactment provides that another enactment applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other enactment is applicable to the matter`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44 the other enactment applies` `the enactment provides that another enactment applies` `the other enactment is applicable to the matter` MEANS
    IF   `the enactment provides that another enactment applies`
    THEN `the other enactment is applicable to the matter`
    ELSE `s 44 speaks only of an enactment that provides that another enactment applies`

-- src:446 | 44 If an enactment provides that another enactment applies, it applies with the necessary changes and so far as it is applicable.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 44 (src:446)
GIVEN `the other enactment applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is necessary`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44 the other enactment applies with this change` `the other enactment applies` `the change is necessary` MEANS
    `the other enactment applies` AND `the change is necessary`
